<title>BELGIUM: EU rice experts to discuss aid for producers.</title>
<headline>EU rice experts to discuss aid for producers.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union's rice management committee will on Thursday vote on detailed rules on compensatory aid for producers, an EU official said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;Under the reform of the rice regime there is to be a gradual reduction in the intervention price for rice. EU producers will get area compensatory payments similar to those which apply in the cereals sector,&quot; the official said.</p>
<p>The first area payments are due to be issued for the 1997/98 marketing year.</p>
<p>Rice experts postponed discussion last week but are now expected to reach agreement before the management committee vote, the official said.</p>
<p>--Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6800</p>
</text>
